From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build(ohos): target the API-21 SDK for the OpenHarmony
 product

hvigor resolves compileSdkVersion against the SDK components actually
installed. With an API-21 OpenHarmony SDK (6.0.1.112) the previous value
of 20 fails packaging with "The SDK management mode has changed" /
"Unable to find the following components", since no API-20 components are
present.

Bump compileSdkVersion/targetSdkVersion to 21 and keep
compatibleSdkVersion at 20 so the minimum supported device API is
unchanged. Note HarmonyOS numbers its 6.0 SDK as API 26, so the
harmonyos product's values are left alone.

Validation: Test by packaging servoshell for the openharmony product against an API-21 OpenHarmony SDK (./mach package --ohos; hvigor must resolve the SDK components).
---
 support/openharmony/build-profile.json5 | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/support/openharmony/build-profile.json5 b/support/openharmony/build-profile.json5
index 848dcedb3a3..5fc8af8f9e2 100644
--- a/support/openharmony/build-profile.json5
+++ b/support/openharmony/build-profile.json5
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@
       {
         "name": "default",
         "signingConfig": "default",
-        "compileSdkVersion": 20,
+        "compileSdkVersion": 21,
         "compatibleSdkVersion": 20,
-        "targetSdkVersion": 20,
+        "targetSdkVersion": 21,
         "runtimeOS": "OpenHarmony"
       },
       {
